WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.768
The hard work that I saw my 
dad put into Chinese&nbsp;food

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:04.306
makes me feel really proud.

00:00:04.306 --> 00:00:06.841
Proud that I was lucky enough
 to learn from a master.

00:00:06.841 --> 00:00:09.362
I want people&nbsp;to value it 
the same way that I do.

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:11.239
So what is the value of Chinese food?

00:00:11.239 --> 00:00:12.519
Is it the taste?

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:14.366
Is it the&nbsp;hard work and the training?

00:00:14.366 --> 00:00:17.864
Or is it the dish's history and 
the nostalgia it makes us feel?

00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:20.027
To&nbsp;me, it is all of those things.

00:00:20.027 --> 00:00:23.584
But the value of Chinese food is 
often compared to fast food,

00:00:23.584 --> 00:00:25.205
quick&nbsp;and cheap.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.327
Although we've spent years 
developing skills to cook faster,

00:00:29.327 --> 00:00:31.263
Chinese food isn't fast&nbsp;food.

00:00:31.752 --> 00:00:33.595
It requires skills,

00:00:33.595 --> 00:00:35.191
mastery of ingredients

00:00:35.191 --> 00:00:36.210
and nostalgia.

00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:40.403
Cooking represents all the hard&nbsp;
work and memories that we had,

00:00:40.403 --> 00:00:41.878
learning the art,

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:43.785
mastering the skills

00:00:43.785 --> 00:00:46.544
and understanding the
 history&nbsp;of Chinese food.

00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:48.894
So the next time you visit 
a Chinese restaurant,

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:50.081
just remember.

00:00:50.647 --> 00:00:52.804
It's not just a&nbsp;
plate of fried rice.

00:00:53.148 --> 00:00:54.971
It's so much more than that.

